####################################################################################
#  .gitignore
#
#  .env IS DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED.
#    This is a private repo and the env file is the single source of truth for
#    configuration, so it is tracked. It contains a real database password, real
#    JWT secrets and a real Cloudinary secret.
#
#  ⚠  IF THIS REPO EVER BECOMES PUBLIC, `.env` WILL LEAK EVERYTHING IN IT.
#     Read the "GOING PUBLIC" section at the bottom of this file first.
####################################################################################


# ── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit these, public or private. Huge, and restorable with `npm ci`.
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
.npm
.yarn


# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated by `npm run build`. Never commit.
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo


# ── Test / coverage output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/


# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs can contain tokens, IPs and request bodies.
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
e2e-test-log.json


# ── Local PGlite database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A real database on disk. Deleting this is fine, `npm run db:up` rebuilds it.
pglite-data/
.pglite.pid
.pglite.log


# ── Uploads ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠  THE MOST IMPORTANT ENTRY IN THIS FILE FOR A LIVE DEPLOY.
#   Render's disk is ephemeral, so nothing here survives a restart anyway. More
#   importantly this holds KYC documents and passport photos. If it is ever
#   committed, treat those as compromised.
uploads/
tmp/
temp/


# ── Caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
.eslintcache
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo


# ── OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini


# ── Credentials that have no business in any repo ───────────────────────────
# Per-developer overrides. The shared .env stays tracked; anything genuinely
# personal goes here and stays local.
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Anything you drop in here stays untracked. Put your own keys here and add
# `!.gitkeep` if you want the folder to exist.
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519


####################################################################################
#  GOING PUBLIC — read this before creating the public/live repo
####################################################################################
#
#  For the public repo, keep every rule above and add these four lines. That
#  strips the credentials while leaving the config structure and all comments
#  intact, so `npm run env:sync` still works for other developers.
#
#      .env
#      .env.local
#      *.pem
#      secrets/
#
#  Then, before the first public push, do all of this — a secret cannot be
#  un-leaked by deleting it in a later commit:
#
#    1. Rotate the database password on Render (Credential Rotation). Anyone who
#       cloned the private repo has it.
#    2. Rotate both JWT secrets. Anyone holding them can mint a token for any
#       account, including SUPER_ADMIN.
#    3. Rotate the Cloudinary API secret and delete the old key.
#    4. Rotate the super admin password (SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD in .env is only
#       applied by `npm run seed` on first run — it does not update an existing
#       row).
#    5. Run `npm run doctor` to confirm nothing weak or public is left.
#
#  `.env.example` is safe to publish only if it holds placeholders. If it holds
#  real values — as it does here — treat it with the same rules as `.env`.
####################################################################################
